Two refinements matter in practice. First, **migratetypes** (`MIGRATE_UNMOVABLE`, `MIGRATE_MOVABLE`, `MIGRATE_RECLAIMABLE`) partition free lists so that unmov able kernel objects do not sit among reclaimable page-cache frames; this preserves the kernel's ability to compact memory by migration. Second, **fallback orders** allow high-order allocations to degrade gracefully: if no order-10 block exists, the allocator may satisfy the request from smaller blocks rather than fail, at the cost of later fragmentation.

